    {
      "title": "Groww Q2 results: Net profit rises 54% to ₹725 crore, revenue up 44%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/groww-q2-results-net-profit-rises-54-to-725-crore-revenue-up-44-126101400593_1.html",
      "description": "Billionbrains Garage Ventures, the parent company of stockbroking platform Groww, on Wednesday reported a 54 per cent year-on-year jump in profit after tax to Rs 725 crore in the September quarter of FY27, driven by higher income and increased contributions from multiple business segments.\nThe company had posted a profit after tax of Rs 471.34 crore in the year-ago period.\nTotal income for the July-September quarter of FY27 rose 44 per cent to Rs 1,540.54 crore, compared with Rs 1,071 crore in the corresponding period last year, the Bengaluru-headquartered company said in a stock exchange filing.\nThe company reported increased contributions from most of its products, including the margin trading facility (MTF) and commodity derivatives.\nHowever, contribution of equity derivatives to total income declined year-on-year, reflecting market adjustments following the introduction of the Closing Auction System (CAS).\n\"We believe this will recover once the recommendations from Sebi's ...",
